# Half-Life 9mm pistol (a Glock 17). Measured by vrcardgen, carved by hand.
#
# THIS MODEL HAS NO MAGAZINE. Posing the reload animation frame by frame,
# nothing on this pistol moves more than 2.2 units, and that is the slide -
# no magazine leaves the gun and none comes back. The grip is 44 vertices,
# because the hand mesh covers it and the artist never modelled what nobody
# would see.
#
# So the magazine is CARVED OUT OF THE GRIP. The 36 vertices in the bottom of
# the grip column get their own bone, and that bone slides out the bottom the
# way a Glock magazine does. Nothing else about the model changes: the same
# geometry sits in the same places, and the surgery is refused outright if it
# cannot do that.
#
# The `match` line is the fingerprint of the model BEFORE surgery, because
# that is the model the engine has when it decides whether this card applies.

weapon v_9mmhandgun
match  bones 36  seqs 9  hash 0xc8430223

# The bone every position in this card is measured in - the controls, the
# grab points, the chamber, the ejection port. Nothing recorded it until
# the engine had to place a control in the world to ask whether a thumb is
# near it; the simulator never needed one, because it never works in world
# space. Taken from the generator, which has always called this bone the
# WEAPON BODY and is what measured these numbers in the first place.
body   "Hands mesh"

type   magazine_slide  capacity 17  rpm 400

# The magazine, cut from the grip. The box is in the body bone's own space,
# which is what the generator's preview draws; the pivot is the top of the
# cut, so the part hinges on nothing and simply slides; and the axis runs
# down the grip, which on this rig is local +Y.
synth magazine  from "Hands mesh"
      box   -0.80 2.15 -0.90   1.15 3.00 1.30
      pivot  0.17 2.21 0.22
      axis   0.0 1.0 0.0   travel 5.00

# The slide. Measured at 3.29 units, moving in reload and shoot_empty -
# which is to say it locks back when the last round goes.
joint 0  bone "Hands mesh 2"  slide  travel 3.29  rest 0
    grab  point 0.09 0.64 1.10  radius 2.5

# ...and the magazine it now has.
joint 1  bone "magazine"  slide  travel 5.00  rest 0
    grab  point 0.17 2.60 0.22  radius 2.0

# `Hands mesh 3` is the hammer: it sits above the bore line at the rear and
# turns a hundred degrees about the lateral axis, only in reload and
# shoot_empty. Not declared, because a hammer nobody can cock is a part the
# simulator would freeze where a hand cannot reach it - it keeps the
# animation it has until there is a control for it.

# THE SLIDE STOP AND THE MAGAZINE RELEASE, ported from cards/hd/v_9mmhandgun
# on 2 Oct 2026 - the same weapon on a remeshed rig.
#
# WHY A PORT IS DEFENSIBLE HERE: identical bone names ("Hands mesh",
# "Hands mesh 2"), and the slide's centroid sits (-0.06 2.41 2.01) from the
# body bone on this rig against (-0.20 2.22 2.70) on HD. The rigs agree to
# within 0.7 units.
#
# WHY 0.7 UNITS IS STILL A RISK: a control is a thumb test. If the thumb
# never lands, these two numbers are the first thing to re-measure on THIS
# file - vr_diag prints the distance, so read it rather than guessing again.
# Part G: a control only ever RELEASES a catch, never engages one.
control slide_lock  at 1.10 -2.79 0.19   finger thumb  kind button
control mag_latch   at 1.08 -0.73 -0.31  finger thumb  kind button
